IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc3-sch1-interpretation`
IMPORT `uc3-sch1-payments`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 4 (housing costs element for renters): paragraph 3 (relevant payments),
-- paragraph 5 (Part 3), paragraph 6 (relevant payments to be taken into account) and paragraph 7 (relevant payments calculated monthly).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1.
--
-- The payment, liability and occupation conditions of paragraph 6(1) are the conditions that regulation 25(5) sets (piece uc1); here they are
-- three stated inputs on each liability. The monthly equivalent of a payment is the keel's table; where the arrangements provide for rent free
-- periods, the text gives the number of payments in a 12 month period by formulas that are missing from this text (fork U3-F1), so that number
-- is a stated input.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 3(1): relevant payments are rent payments (Schedule 1 paragraph 2) and service charge payments (Schedule 1 paragraph 7, and, in the
-- social rented sector, paragraph 8, whose conditions the payment record already carries: Sch 1 para 8(1)).
-- src:2168 | (1) “Relevant payments” means one or more payments of any of the following descriptions—
-- src:2169 | (a) rent payments;
-- src:2170 | (b) service charge payments.
-- src:2171 | (2) “Rent payments”, in relation to any calculation under Part 4 or 5 of this Schedule, has the meaning given in paragraph 2 of Schedule 1.
-- src:2172 | (3) “Service charge payments”—
-- src:2173 | (a) for the purposes of calculations under Part 4 of this Schedule, has the meaning given in paragraph 7 of Schedule 1;
-- src:2174 | (b) for the purposes of calculations under Part 5 of this Schedule, is to be understood in accordance with paragraphs 7 and 8 of Schedule 1.
@ref Sch 4 para 3 (src:2168-2174)
DECLARE `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation` HAS
    payment                                                                                                      IS A `Payment in respect of accommodation`
    `amount of each payment in pounds`                                                                           IS A NUMBER
    `how often the payment falls due`                                                                            IS A `Payment interval`
    -- out of range: reg 25(5) (piece uc1)
    `the renter meets the payment condition in respect of the description of relevant payment`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the renter meets the liability condition in respect of the description of relevant payment`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the renter meets the occupation condition in respect of the description of relevant payment`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payment has already been brought into account in relation to the same or a different renter`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangements provide for one or more rent free periods`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `total number of the relevant payments which the renter is liable to make in that 12 month period`           IS A NUMBER

-- src:2168 | (1) “Relevant payments” means one or more payments of any of the following descriptions—
-- src:2169 | (a) rent payments;
-- src:2170 | (b) service charge payments.
-- src:2171 | (2) “Rent payments”, in relation to any calculation under Part 4 or 5 of this Schedule, has the meaning given in paragraph 2 of Schedule 1.
-- src:2172 | (3) “Service charge payments”—
-- src:2173 | (a) for the purposes of calculations under Part 4 of this Schedule, has the meaning given in paragraph 7 of Schedule 1;
-- src:2174 | (b) for the purposes of calculations under Part 5 of this Schedule, is to be understood in accordance with paragraphs 7 and 8 of Schedule 1.
@ref Sch 4 para 3(1) to (3) (src:2168-2174)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 3 — the payment is a relevant payment` liability MEANS
    (`Sch 1 para 2 — a rent payment` (liability's payment))
    OR (`Sch 1 para 7(1) — a service charge payment` ((liability's payment)'s `the payment as a possible service charge payment`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 6(1): a description of relevant payment is taken into account where the renter meets all three conditions in respect of it.
-- src:2189 | (1) Where a renter meets the payment condition, liability condition and occupation condition in respect of one or more descriptions of relevant payment, each such description is to be taken into account for the purposes of the calculation under Part 4 or 5 of this Schedule.
@ref Sch 4 para 6(1) (src:2189)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 6(1) — the renter meets the payment, liability and occupation conditions` liability MEANS
    (liability's `the renter meets the payment condition in respect of the description of relevant payment`)
    AND (liability's `the renter meets the liability condition in respect of the description of relevant payment`)
    AND (liability's `the renter meets the occupation condition in respect of the description of relevant payment`)

-- Paragraphs 6(1) to (3): a liability is brought into account if it is a relevant payment, meets the three conditions, and has not already
-- been brought into account. "To the extent that" in paragraph 6(2) is read as: the amount entered is the amount that meets the conditions (fork U3-F13).
-- src:2189 | (1) Where a renter meets the payment condition, liability condition and occupation condition in respect of one or more descriptions of relevant payment, each such description is to be taken into account for the purposes of the calculation under Part 4 or 5 of this Schedule.
-- src:2190 | (2) No account is to be taken of any amount of a relevant payment to the extent that all of the conditions referred to in sub-paragraph (1) are not met in respect of that amount.
-- src:2191 | (3) Any particular payment for which a renter is liable is not to be brought into account more than once, whether in relation to the same or a different renter (but this does not prevent different payments of the same description being brought into account in respect of an assessment period).
@ref Sch 4 para 6(1) to (3) (src:2189-2191)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 6 — the liability is brought into account` liability MEANS
    (`Sch 4 para 3 — the payment is a relevant payment` liability)
    AND (`Sch 4 para 6(1) — the renter meets the payment, liability and occupation conditions` liability)
    AND (NOT (liability's `the payment has already been brought into account in relation to the same or a different renter`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 7: the monthly amount. Where the period of liability is not a month, the monthly equivalent of the keel's table (7(2)); where the
-- arrangements provide for rent free periods, the amount times the number of payments in 12 months, divided by 12 (7(3), 7(3A) formulas absent).
-- src:2193 | (1) Where any relevant payment is to be taken into account under paragraph 6, the amount of that payment is to be calculated as a monthly amount.
-- src:2194 | (2) Where the period in respect of which a renter is liable to make a relevant payment is not a month, an amount is to be calculated as the monthly equivalent, so for example—
-- src:2195 | (a) weekly payments are multiplied by 52 and divided by 12;
-- src:2196 | (aa) two-weekly payments are multiplied by 26 and divided by 12;
-- src:2197 | (b) four-weekly payments are multiplied by 13 and divided by 12;
-- src:2198 | (c) three-monthly payments are multiplied by 4 and divided by 12; and
-- src:2199 | (d) annual payments are divided by 12.
-- src:2200 | (3) Where a renter is liable for relevant payments under arrangements that provide for one or more rent free periods, subject to sub-paragraph (3A), the monthly equivalent is to be calculated over 12 months by reference to the total number of relevant payments which the renter is liable to make in that 12 month period.
@ref Sch 4 para 7(1) to (3) (src:2193-2200)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      interval IS A `Payment interval`
      `the arrangements provide for one or more rent free periods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `total number of the relevant payments which the renter is liable to make in that 12 month period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 7 — the monthly equivalent of an amount` amount interval `the arrangements provide for one or more rent free periods` `total number of the relevant payments which the renter is liable to make in that 12 month period` MEANS
    IF `the arrangements provide for one or more rent free periods`
    THEN (amount TIMES `total number of the relevant payments which the renter is liable to make in that 12 month period`) DIVIDED BY 12
    ELSE `core — the monthly equivalent of a payment` amount interval

-- src:2193 | (1) Where any relevant payment is to be taken into account under paragraph 6, the amount of that payment is to be calculated as a monthly amount.
-- src:2194 | (2) Where the period in respect of which a renter is liable to make a relevant payment is not a month, an amount is to be calculated as the monthly equivalent, so for example—
-- src:2195 | (a) weekly payments are multiplied by 52 and divided by 12;
-- src:2196 | (aa) two-weekly payments are multiplied by 26 and divided by 12;
-- src:2197 | (b) four-weekly payments are multiplied by 13 and divided by 12;
-- src:2198 | (c) three-monthly payments are multiplied by 4 and divided by 12; and
-- src:2199 | (d) annual payments are divided by 12.
-- src:2200 | (3) Where a renter is liable for relevant payments under arrangements that provide for one or more rent free periods, subject to sub-paragraph (3A), the monthly equivalent is to be calculated over 12 months by reference to the total number of relevant payments which the renter is liable to make in that 12 month period.
@ref Sch 4 para 7(1) to (3) (src:2193-2200)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 7 — the monthly equivalent of a liability` liability MEANS
    `Sch 4 para 7 — the monthly equivalent of an amount` (liability's `amount of each payment in pounds`) (liability's `how often the payment falls due`) (liability's `the arrangements provide for one or more rent free periods`) (liability's `total number of the relevant payments which the renter is liable to make in that 12 month period`)

-- src:2189 | (1) Where a renter meets the payment condition, liability condition and occupation condition in respect of one or more descriptions of relevant payment, each such description is to be taken into account for the purposes of the calculation under Part 4 or 5 of this Schedule.
-- src:2190 | (2) No account is to be taken of any amount of a relevant payment to the extent that all of the conditions referred to in sub-paragraph (1) are not met in respect of that amount.
-- src:2191 | (3) Any particular payment for which a renter is liable is not to be brought into account more than once, whether in relation to the same or a different renter (but this does not prevent different payments of the same description being brought into account in respect of an assessment period).
-- src:2193 | (1) Where any relevant payment is to be taken into account under paragraph 6, the amount of that payment is to be calculated as a monthly amount.
@ref Sch 4 para 6 and para 7(1) (src:2189-2191) (src:2193)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 6 — the monthly amount of a liability taken into account` liability MEANS
    IF `Sch 4 para 6 — the liability is brought into account` liability
    THEN `Sch 4 para 7 — the monthly equivalent of a liability` liability
    ELSE 0

-- src:2189 | (1) Where a renter meets the payment condition, liability condition and occupation condition in respect of one or more descriptions of relevant payment, each such description is to be taken into account for the purposes of the calculation under Part 4 or 5 of this Schedule.
-- src:2190 | (2) No account is to be taken of any amount of a relevant payment to the extent that all of the conditions referred to in sub-paragraph (1) are not met in respect of that amount.
-- src:2191 | (3) Any particular payment for which a renter is liable is not to be brought into account more than once, whether in relation to the same or a different renter (but this does not prevent different payments of the same description being brought into account in respect of an assessment period).
-- src:2192 | 7 Relevant payments calculated monthly
-- src:2193 | (1) Where any relevant payment is to be taken into account under paragraph 6, the amount of that payment is to be calculated as a monthly amount.
@ref Sch 4 para 6 and para 7(1) (src:2189-2193)
GIVEN liabilities IS A LIST OF `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 6 — the monthly amount of all the relevant payments taken into account` liabilities MEANS
    sum (map `Sch 4 para 6 — the monthly amount of a liability taken into account` liabilities)

-- Paragraph 7(4): a rent free period is a period in respect of which the renter has no liability to make one or more of the relevant payments
-- taken into account under paragraph 6.
-- src:2206 | (4) “Rent free period” means any period in respect of which the renter has no liability to make one or more of the relevant payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6.
@ref Sch 4 para 7(4) (src:2206)
DECLARE `Period of the arrangements` HAS
    `the renter has no liability in respect of the period to make one or more of the relevant payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2206 | (4) “Rent free period” means any period in respect of which the renter has no liability to make one or more of the relevant payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6.
@ref Sch 4 para 7(4) (src:2206)
GIVEN period IS A `Period of the arrangements`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 7(4) — a rent free period` period MEANS
    period's `the renter has no liability in respect of the period to make one or more of the relevant payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6`
